The model number would help, but it sounds like you got a Multia/UDB
(looks like a pizza box). Model numbers on them begin with VX40, VX41,
or VX42.  Since you will be running Linux on it, call it a UDB (Universal
Desktop Box).  Multia refers to the box with Multia software on it -
basically NT 3.5 with some Digital networking addons.

Assuming you have a web browser available, surf over to:

   http://www.dcginc.com/linux.htm

where there are step-by-step instructions for loading RedHat Linux.
Should apply to any other Alpha distribution though.

