This should be a standard feature of ATX power supplies.  This is the
"softpower" annoyance.	The MB itself actually requires that that the
softpower pins toggle states to turn it on or off.

If you short them, the machine will turn on.
Unshort while on- nothing
short again- off

Repeat as needed ;)

There may be a way to disable this on some boards, but to my knowledge, my
PC164LX does not have any way to disable it.

/Mike

