Could anyone explain this odd behaviour of 164LX?

We get machine check 670 errors in AlphaPC 164LX with 4MB cache.
Errors occur when Linux (RH 4.2) is starting network (DEC 21041 Tulip 
driver) or in SRM when one or more commands are given (for example show 
config causes crash every time, others when repeated many times).
After booting, Linux seems to work normally, even the network connection.

I guess those errors have something to do with cache, because SRM errors
disappear when cache is jumpered to 0 MB. Maybe 4 MB cache is not
completely supported? Jumpering cache size to 2 MB doesn't help.
Processor speed at 466, 533 or 600 MHz doesn't matter.

