Hi !

I bought a VX40 (multia) recently. I am having trouble to get it 
to network. I am using Thinwire (10base2), and have verified that 
the network works with other machies. The alpha runs kernel 2.0.33.

The network chip is a 21040. When I use the tulip.c driver, it 
recognizes the chip, complains that it doesn't have 10baseT, 
switches to 10base2 and then nothing.. Tcpdumping on another 
machine shows absolutely not traffic from my new alpha.

The de4x5.c driver does the same, except that I see I packet full of
zeros addressed to itself when tcpdumping on another machine. Tcpdump 
on the alpha only shows traffic originating locally (i.e. on the alpha).

I also tried forcing both drivers to 10base2, but to no avail.

Does anybody have any suggestions? Is it possible to screw up networking 
in the SRM. (I bought the machine 2nd hand, so I am not exactly sure 
about what happened to it before...)

TIA,

Bart

