I recently told here that I had problems installing RH5.0 via FTP. Now I
found the solution. Took me 4 days.
The eth0 driver in 2.0.33 (tulip) seems not to be able to autoprobe which
connection (thinwire, aui or twisted).
So I used the old kernel from RH4.2 which uses another driver . If I
remember right it is DExxx something.

So what I have done is.
Booted with milo, then booted the old image and used the new ramdisk.
Wonder it works.

CU

Patrick




