In article <34c96bc4.1677691@news.mindspring.com> mark_root@yahoo.com writes:

> I have been tring to get Xfree86 to work on the multia[VX40F-F2] w/
> RedHat 5.0 and have not found the proper settings for the Video  &
> what RamDac to choose if any should be selected. 
>
> Please Help

I can't get to my UDB right now, but I recall that the main problem
I had was that with 5.0 you need to specify the MemBase variable in
your XF86Config file.

1) more /proc/pci

2) look for membase under the video listing (mine was 0xa00000 or similar).

3) add "Option MemBase <value>" to the XF86Config file, I believe under
   Default (there are a number of Option lines, goes with them).

4) now try doing 'startx'. It should come right up. RAMDAC, etc. are
   autodetected, so you don't need to set them.

Let me know if this helps.

MarkG
