That is exactly what I have seen when I put SDRAM in an 164LX which is
either too slow (66MHz or buffered), too weak (3 clock vs 4) or not ECC
(may or may not be required in your system).

I do not know what board you have in machine, so I cannot speak to which
of those might be the problem, but bad ram will keep the machine from
doing ANYHTING!!

What brand/speed/parity do you have vs do you need :)

Many lie/fudge, so be carefull Alphas eat cheap ram for breakfast (well,
they barf anyway).

/Mike

