Having bought a Multia recently I wondered if the thing can be booted
diskless from a Linux server. I found the Digital Unix console (which is
an alternative to the ARC console) which can be told to boot using the
networkdevice (EWA0).

I even managed to tell it to use the BOOTP protocol, so I installed a
dhcp server on my (Intel) Linux server to serve up these BOOTP requests.
However when I tell the Multia to boot, it never receives a message from
the BOOTP server (i.e. DHCP server). I checked the configuration of the
DHCP server twice, double checked the fixed Ethernet address and all seem
OK. However, it turns out that the Multia does not receive an answer on
its BOOTP request.

Has anybody succeeded in diskless booting of a Multia (it would make a
nice diskless X terminal)

