I did it. I actually got mMosaic running on an Alpha running Redhat
5.0. This is amazing, because I'm very much a novice. Here's what I had to do:

1) Get "lesstif" and follow the installation instructions. The instructions
are very good, and I had very little trouble. The test examples all worked.

2) set LD_LIBRARY_PATH to point to the lesstif stuff.

3) Get mMosaic unpacked, and do "make linux".

4) Watch it fail to compile.

5) fix several things in the source:

	5a) Some function in stdlib wanted to be declared 
	"extern const char *const mumble()". This was in a
	 lot of places.

	5b) A call to signal had a symbol "SIGCLD" which had to be
	changed to "SIGCHLD". Don't know why is was the way it was.

	5c) replace several calls to gets() with fgets(,n,stdin)

6) Now it compiles and loads.

7) It even runs, but with a lot of warning messages to the shell, and
it sometimes core dumps.

8) Set WWW_HOME to a home page (and export WWW_HOME)

I have not gotten it to read pages from the network yet, just from my machine.

Just thought somebody would like to see what I had to do.....



Ed






