Hmmm ... you know, this is something I noticed on Solaris but it might
be true for Linux/Alpha as well ... when gcc is run as the linker,
look for an '-R' option.  If there is one, get rid of the -R from the
makefile since gcc does something strange with it present on the
command line.

	gcc obj1.o obj2.o -o program -lX11 -R -ldl

for instance will cause gcc to not process the -ldl properly.



