I see two problems here; first you need to append 'prompt_ramdisk=1' to the
command line, otherwise it won't ask you for the ramdisk floppy. Secondly,
Linux kernels up until 2.1.7x or so doesn't handle serial consoles very
well, you need a specially compiled kernel for it. And I don't think that
the RedHat installation works with a serial console.(?)
So use/borrow/steal a keyboard and a monitor long enough so you can install
RedHat and build a new kernel (2.1.76 seems to work fine for me) with
support for the console on the serial port.

/stefan

