Larry Pisani wrote:
> 
> Hello friends,
> 
> I have a 166 multia/udb and I'm trying to load RedHat Linux 5.0/Alpha.
> Well, I finally figured out getting the right milo image, and I can even
> get the boot image disk to work (up to a point).  It seems to hang when
> "jumping to the Linux Kernel" which I THINK is when I expect it to
> prompt me for the root disk.  I think the key here is that I'm booting
> the host from a serial terminal (VT420) no VGA/TGA console.  Has anyone
> come across this with a solution?  Or perhaps a few tips?  Anything at
> this point woule be helpful.  Below is my milo boot command followed
> with a few lines I get just prior to the hanging.
> 

If your kernel does not have TGA or VGA drivers linked in, then this is
the exact place where it seems like it has stalled.  It's really booting
fine.

Have you got all messages coming out the serial port (another
Linux/Alpha kernel configuration option)? My guess is, you've got the
ARC console sending everything out to the serial port, you've got Milo
built from a kernel that echos to the serial port, but your actual
kernel does not, as this is not the default configuration.

Why not just configure-in VGA and TGA?  Then, if you happen to have a
video board at some time, it will boot just fine.

Note that, if you're booting from the ARC console, and there's no
keyboard attached, the ARC console won't automatically boot anything. 
Depending on what you're trying to do with a headless boot... this may
be your next problem.

Chris
