> we are looking for a AXP21164 based system that suport >1GB RAM.
> The RPX164-2 (DeskStation Technologies, Lenexa, Kansas) is such a board,
> but I have not found any information wheter the board and its on board
> components (SCSI, VGA, LAN) are supported by Linux.

The PC164LX is limited to 2 pairs of DIMMS, and "512 MB", although it's
not clear if it would take 256M DIMMS if you wanted to buy 'em.

The PC164UX (Samsung) takes 3 pairs of DIMMS and explicitly says
it would go to 3 GB with 512M DIMMS.

The RXP164-2 has the same limitation. And the same chipset, for core
stuff, I think, but I wouldn't know about LAN or VGA.

-- g




