Deskstation has it's own port of Redhat 4.2 at
ftp://www.deskstation.com/linux/ the onboard SCSI and Ethernet are supported
but the EIDE is not. The RPX164-2 has 3 banks using 6 DIMM slots and can
support 3GB of RAM using 512MB DIMMs, but I don't know if this port supports
this configuration. As far as the motherboard goes I think it supports any
size DIMMs. For more information about the Deskstation port visit
ftp://www.deskstation.com/linux/html/index.html

If you are looking to buy a RPX164-2 I can sell you one, my company is
authorized by Deskstation. I can also sell the Alpha 21164 CPUs 366MHz
through 600MHz and memory for the RPX164-2.

