            Andy Smith <ajs@dca.net> reported some wierd scsi errors,
citing:

scsi0: MEDIUM ERROR on channel 0, id 0, lun 0, CDB: 0x03 00 00 00 10 00
scsidisk I/O error: dev 08:05, sector 639014, absolute sector 2080576

That's a real problem. You have a (potentially) bad spot on the disk. I
don't know if
there is a utility under Linux to revector bad blocks (there is one
under Digital
UNIX), but in the meanwhile, I'd do what I could to back up the data. If
you have
the means to wipe the disk completely, reformat it, and then restore
your data,
that might help, but again, I don't know enough about the innards of the
various
ext2fs utilities to tell you if that would solve the problem. The 1.5 GB
disk - is
that an RZ27? Might be getting old, but I can't be too sure. In any
case, that is a
warning to be taken seriously.


