I realize this is not a good solution for someone who only owns an alpha
and nothing else, but if you just retired a 486 or a slow pentium,
running netscape on that and piping it over to the alpha (via xhost,
SETENV DISPLAY, etc..).

It works well even over 10Mbs!!

*make sure it is full duplex though, netscape likes to talk in both
directions 100Mbs simplex will feel much slower than 10Mbs FD, so it is
important!!

Might as well put that lame duck to some good use.  It is more than
adequate(stuff it with ram of course, netscape loves to chew up ram). 
Keeps wastefull browser code out of your nice Alpha memory space (which
generally comes at a premium price:))

You can use chinsy video cards(only enough to boot into text mode, no
sound card, very small hard drives.

Heck, spend some time figuring out how to get bootp running and use no
hard drive (my next step)!

With some rsh commands, some scripts for dealing with remote sysadmin and
a good button bar, you can get things running such that you don't even
know that you are using two computers, other than the annoying hum and
the power bill!!!! :(

Just had not heard anyone mention this as a fun to impliment fix for the
lack of a native GUI browser for alpha, but it seemed like many of the
postings implied that people had access to now idle x86 hardware.

Not to mention that this is a nice solution for running __anything__ that
will not run/compile on alpha while you spend time figuring out how to
make it compile on alpha ;).

Just a thought,

