[snip]
: The egcs/g77 code took 50.7 seconds to execute in 32bit arithmetic and 51.4
: seconds in 64 bit arithmetic (does this mean that their 32bit cos routine
: actually uses the 64bit routine?).

Actually, they both use the 80 bit routine.  The transcendental functions
provided by the 387 FPU are always done in extended double precision mode
in the FPU's stack (regardless of the precision setting of the FPU). 

