There are a number of "document processing" options for Linux; see:
<http://www.hex.net/~cbbrowne/wp.html>

There are credible commercial "word processors" for the Intel architecture,
namely Applix Word, StarOffice Word, and WordPerfect.  They may run on Linux
Alpha via the EM86 "emulator."

The "free" options are generally less credible in terms of:

a) General adoption within the community

(how many users are there for EZ?)

b) Interoperability with Windows-based word processors

(The Windows environment is clearly an application "wasteland" as there is
only one word processor that anyone cares about, namely Word, and only one
spreadsheet that anyone cares about, namely Excel, and trash bins filled
with other worthless software...)


