> arrow is over rather than having to "click" to atcivated a window. Can
> this be changed

Yes. I assume that you are running fvwm/fvwm95. Take a look at the man page
for fvwm (man fvwm). There is a style option called ClickToFocus. I think
the default resource file sets it to MouseFocus. You need to change it to
the above option. 
 
> 
> 2) can I set up the a: drive .I'm tired of having to ftp stuff to the
> server reboot into nt and ftp backdown
> 

I have not clearly understood what you want. If you are looking for a way to
read floppies, it is fairly simple. You can mount dos, ext2 and probably 100
other filesystem and read/write on it. Take a look at the man pages for mount
(man mount). The device is normally /dev/fd0. Alternatively, you can read and
write into an unformattted floppy using the tar (man tar for details).

One advice to you is that get a good book on Linux (Running Linux by Matt
Welsh, for instance) and learn the general concepts for the  Linux/Unix
operating system.  That way, you will find it a lot less frustrating.

Regards. 

