Kevin Gross <root@sprynet.com> wrote:
: Is it possible to get dosemu and/or Wine on a PC164 LX under linux?  If
: so, can someone point me in the right direction for making it work?  I
: have got the sources, but when I try to 'make' them, they both complain.
: Dosemu needs as86 or ld86 for assembling the dosemu BIOS.  I'm not sure
: what these are or how to get them.  Wine quits about half way through the
: 'make depend; make' when it says

: make[1]: *** [lstr.o] Error 1
: make[1]: Leaving directory '/root/wine/wine971221/misc'
: make: *** [misc] Error 2 

: Do dosemu and wine only run on x86 architecture or will they work on the
: DEC Alpha?

Both dosemu and wine don't have binary emulation. So you can't use
them. You can try to run wine with EM86, but not dosemu, as it needs vm86
(16 bit) mode. 

I think it would be worth working on wine with EM86. If I remember right,
the EM86 people told that they would be willing to add needed features to
run wine. But probably it will be a lot of work.

