Hello,

I'm trying to install Linux 4.2 Alpha on a Microway Screamer 21164 Alpha

station.  I followed directions and made a MILO boot disk from the
image.  I've added a "Linux" entry under Alpha BIOS pointing to
linload.exe on the diskette.  However, the machine locks up when booting

from the MILO diskette with a message "Swapping PALcode".  I've tried
all the boot images, but none of them worked.  The manual for Alpha
RedHat said that Microway Screamers are eb164.img compatible.
Apparently, they're not.  The Alpha BIOS is of October '97.
Anybody have a solution?

Thanks very much.
